.TH RINGS 1 "September 2026" "rings 0.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rings \- DaisyDisk-style terminal disk-usage map
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rings [options] [path]
.PP
.B rings help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rings
scans a directory (or a single file) and shows a DaisyDisk-style radial
sunburst of disk use beside a largest-first list. Each wedge is a file
or folder, sized by what it uses on disk. Click or keyboard-select a
wedge or row, drill in, mark waste, and delete only after an explicit
confirm. Nothing is removed while you browse.
.PP
Given a
.IR path ,
rings scans it immediately. Started with no path in a terminal, it
opens a directory picker in the current directory; pick a directory
and press
.B s
to scan it. Piped or scripted runs with no path still scan the current
directory.
.PP
When stdout is not a terminal (a pipe or redirect), rings prints a
plain table automatically. The scripting flags
.BR \-\-plain ,
.BR \-\-csv ,
and
.B \-\-json
never enter the TUI, even in a terminal.
.PP
The scan stays on one filesystem by default, skips Linux virtual mounts
(\fI/proc\fP, \fI/sys\fP, \fI/dev\fP, \fI/run\fP), never follows
symlinked directories, and counts hard-linked inodes once. Without
root it scans what it can read.
.PP
Press
.B ?
or
.B F1
in the TUI for the full key list.
.B rings help
and
.B rings \-\-help
print the same list on stdout.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I path
Directory or file to scan.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Write the analyzed tree as JSON to stdout and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-csv \ file
Write findings CSV to
.I file
and exit (written to a temp name, then renamed).
.TP
.BR \-\-plain ", " \-\-no\-tui
Print a parseable tab-separated table to stdout and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Skip the GitHub Release update check that an interactive TUI launch
otherwise runs.
.TP
.B \-\-one\-file\-system
Stay on one filesystem (default).
.TP
.B \-\-all\-filesystems
Descend into other mounted filesystems.
.TP
.B \-\-apparent
Size by apparent bytes (st_size) instead of used blocks.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme \ name
Color theme:
.BR rings " (default),"
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR solarized\-dark ,
.BR mono .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " help
Print the logo, usage, and every key binding.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.B rings help
is the canonical key list. A short summary:
.TP
.B j k
Move the selection (also arrows, Page Up/Down,
.BR g / G
for first/last).
.TP
.B Enter
Drill into the selected directory.
.TP
.B h
Go up one directory (also Backspace).
.TP
.B \-
Reopen the directory picker.
.TP
.B Space
Mark or unmark for delete.
.TP
.B f
Temp and cache findings.
.TP
.B c
Delete collector.
.TP
.B x
Confirm deletion from the collector. As root you must type DELETE;
as a user, items go to trash.
.TP
.B e
Export the current view to CSV.
.TP
.BR ? ", " F1
Help overlay.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.PP
Mouse: click selects, double-click drills in, right-click opens a
context menu, the wheel scrolls, hover highlights.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RINGS_NO_UPDATE
Set to 1 to skip the GitHub Release update check (same as
.BR \-\-offline ).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable color (bold and reverse video only).
.TP
.B RINGS_COLORS
Override color-depth detection:
.BR 16 ,
.BR 256 ,
or
.BR truecolor .
.TP
.B COLORTERM
Used with the terminal type to detect 24-bit color.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Scan or I/O failure.
.TP
.B 2
Unknown option or other usage error.
.SH FILES
CSV export columns are
.IR path , type , size_bytes , size_human , category
and, for
.BR \-\-csv ,
.IR in_delete_collector .
Every directory, every temp/cache/log/journal/crash hit, and every
file of 1 MiB or more is included; tiny ordinary files are omitted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Scan the whole disk (needs root for a complete picture):
.B sudo rings /
.TP
Scan a single tree:
.B rings /var/log
.TP
Parseable table, no TUI:
.B rings \-\-plain /
.TP
JSON of the analyzed tree:
.B rings \-\-json /srv
.TP
Findings CSV for scripts:
.B rings \-\-csv findings.csv /
.TP
TUI without the update check:
.B rings \-\-offline /home
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR du (1),
.BR df (1),
.BR ncdu (1)
